  "question": {
    "text": "The rate of a reaction quadruples when the temperature changes from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>300</mi><mi>&#8201;</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>310</mn><mo>&#8201;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> . The activation energy of this reaction is:<br /><br />(Assume Activation energy and pre-exponential factor are independent of temperature; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>693</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"
