  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The activation energy, rate constant and temperature can be related using Arrhenius equation.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>Ae</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mi>RT</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>300</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>310</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>693</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>300</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>310</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.